%% Pudel Authentication Flow v2.5.0 (cookie-only BFF)
%% No token, key id, or proof ever reaches the browser. Only the AES-GCM
%% encrypted HttpOnly session cookie crosses the wire, and the DPoP proof is
%% minted and validated inside the BFF on every request.

sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant User as User
    participant Vue as Vue Frontend
    participant API as Pudel API
    participant Filter as JwtAuthenticationFilter
    participant Cookie as SessionCookieService
    participant KeyMgr as DPoPKeyManager
    participant DB as PostgreSQL
    participant Discord as Discord OAuth2
    participant DPoP as DPoPService

    Note over User,Discord: Step 0: Bootstrap the encrypted browser session

    User->>Vue: Open the dashboard
    Vue->>API: GET /api/session/bootstrap<br/>credentials: include
    API->>Cookie: readKeyId(request)
    alt Existing cookie resolves to an active key row
        Cookie-->>API: keyId
    else No cookie / expired / unknown key
        API->>KeyMgr: createSessionKey()
        KeyMgr->>KeyMgr: Ed25519 KeyPairGenerator
        KeyMgr->>DB: INSERT dpop_keys (user_id=anonymous,<br/>public and private JWK, thumbprint, expires_at)
        KeyMgr-->>API: keyId
    end
    API->>Cookie: writeCookie(response, keyId, expiresAt)
    Note right of Cookie: HttpOnly, Secure, SameSite=Strict, path=/<br/>value = base64url(iv).base64url(AES-GCM ciphertext)<br/>plaintext = { v:1, keyId, exp }
    API-->>Vue: 200 { ready, expiresAt, maxAgeSeconds }
    Note right of Vue: No keyId, no JWT, nothing stored in localStorage

    Note over User,Discord: Step 1: Discord OAuth2 login

    User->>Vue: Click "Login with Discord"
    Vue->>Discord: Redirect to OAuth2 authorize
    Discord->>User: Consent screen
    User->>Discord: Approve
    Discord->>Vue: Redirect with code
    Vue->>API: POST /api/auth/discord/callback<br/>Cookie: pudel_session=..., Body: { code, redirectUri }

    API->>Cookie: readKeyId(httpRequest)
    API->>KeyMgr: findActiveSession(keyId)
    KeyMgr->>DB: SELECT ... WHERE key_id = ? AND is_active<br/>AND expires_at > now()
    alt No active browser session
        API-->>Vue: 401 { error: "Missing or invalid browser session" }
    end

    API->>Discord: Exchange code for tokens
    Discord-->>API: access_token, refresh_token, expires_in
    API->>Discord: GET /users/@me
    Discord-->>API: User info (id, username, avatar)
    API->>DB: Upsert users + user_guilds, store Discord tokens
    API->>KeyMgr: getPublicKeyThumbprint(browserKeyId)
    API->>API: JwtUtil.generateDPoPBoundToken(userId,<br/>{ username }, thumbprint)
    Note right of API: EdDSA signed, claims: sub, iat, exp,<br/>cnf = { "jkt": "<RFC 7638 thumbprint>" }
    API->>KeyMgr: bindSessionKey(browserKeyId, userId, jwt)
    KeyMgr->>DB: UPDATE dpop_keys SET user_id, access_token
    API-->>Vue: 200 { accessToken: null, user: {...}, tokenType: "COOKIE" }

    Note over User,Discord: Step 2: Protected resource request (no client credential)

    User->>Vue: Open guild settings
    Vue->>Filter: GET /api/guilds/{guildId}/settings<br/>Cookie only - no Authorization header

    Filter->>Filter: Authorization header present?
    Note right of Filter: Any Authorization header is rejected outright:<br/>401 { "error": "invalid_token" }

    Filter->>Cookie: readKeyId(request) - decrypt AES-GCM
    Cookie-->>Filter: keyId
    Filter->>KeyMgr: findActiveSession(keyId)
    KeyMgr-->>Filter: DPoPKey row (access_token)
    Filter->>Filter: JwtUtil.validateToken(accessToken)
    Note right of Filter: EdDSA signature + exp verified with<br/>keys/pb.key (public)

    Filter->>KeyMgr: signInternalProof(keyId, method, uri, token)
    Note right of KeyMgr: payload = { jti, htm, htu, iat, ath }<br/>ath = base64url(SHA-256(accessToken))<br/>header = { typ: dpop-proof, alg: EdDSA, jwk }
    KeyMgr-->>Filter: Signed internal proof

    Filter->>DPoP: validateProofForResource(proof, method, uri, token, keyId)
    Note right of DPoP: alg must be EdDSA / htm == method /<br/>htu == host and port and path / abs(iat - now) <= 60s /<br/>jti unused (per-keyId ledger) / ath == SHA-256(token)
    DPoP-->>Filter: valid + thumbprint

    Filter->>Filter: cnf.jkt of accessToken == proof thumbprint?<br/>token sub == dpop_keys.user_id?
    Filter->>Filter: set auth = UsernamePasswordAuthenticationToken(userId,<br/>authorities = [DPOP_VERIFIED])<br/>request attr pudel.session.keyId = keyId
    Filter-->>Vue: 200 + guild settings

    Note over User,Discord: Step 3: Silent refresh (SPA reacts to one 401)

    Vue->>API: POST /api/auth/refresh<br/>Cookie only
    API->>Cookie: readKeyId(request)
    API->>KeyMgr: findActiveSession(keyId)
    API->>DB: Refresh Discord token if expiring within 300s
    API->>KeyMgr: generateDPoPBoundToken(...) + storeAccessToken(keyId, jwt)
    API-->>Vue: 200 { accessToken: null, user: {...}, tokenType: "COOKIE" }
    Note right of Vue: One retry per request, on failure only<br/>non-sensitive UI state (user, admin_info) is cleared

    Note over User,Discord: Step 4: Restore after a page refresh

    Vue->>API: GET /api/auth/me (Cookie only)
    API->>KeyMgr: findActiveSession(keyId).access_token
    API-->>Vue: 200 UserDto

    Note over User,Discord: Step 5: Logout

    Vue->>API: POST /api/auth/logout (Cookie only)
    API->>KeyMgr: clearKeyPair(keyId)
    KeyMgr->>DB: UPDATE dpop_keys SET is_active = false
    API->>Cookie: clearCookie(response)
    Note right of Cookie: HttpOnly, Secure, SameSite=Strict, Max-Age=0
    API-->>Vue: 200 { message: "Logged out successfully" }

    Note over User,Discord: Key rotation (explicit)

    Vue->>API: POST /api/session/rotate
    API->>KeyMgr: createSessionKey() - new Ed25519 key
    API->>Cookie: writeCookie(new keyId)
    API-->>Vue: 200 { ready, expiresAt }
    Note right of API: Tokens bound to the old key id stop working